      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Sertraline's maximum recommended adult dose is 200 mg per day. An order for 1000 mg is five times that. It could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity (QT prolongation). The patient's normal kidney and liver function doesn't change this. It may be a typo, for example 100 mg entered as 1000 mg.\n\n2. **Medication orders need a prescriber.** You've said you're not a clinician. A licensed prescriber should place or verify the order, and a pharmacist normally reviews it too.\n\nPlease ask the treating clinician to confirm the intended dose. Typical adult dosing is 25\u201350 mg once daily at the start, titrated up to 200 mg once daily at most. If they confirm a corrected dose within the usual range, I can enter it then. If the 1000 mg dose really is intended, it needs direct prescriber and pharmacy verification first."
      }
